8 questions, 3 runs each — 24 answers

  first answer     figure 24/24   cause 21/24    3,281 tokens/answer
  after a critic   figure 24/24   cause 21/24    5,686 tokens/answer

  accuracy 94% -> 94%   for 1.7x the tokens
  the critic found something to say 15 times, and passed 9

It changed nothing at all, for 1.7x the tokens.

The critic objected 15 times out of 24 and passed the other 9. Every one of
those objections cost a second full answer.

That is consistent with §9.5, where reflection scored worst of the six
prompting patterns, and the reason is the same. The mistakes here are not
visible in the output: a cause that is subtly the wrong quarter reads
perfectly well. Checking it means searching the documents again, which is not
reviewing — it is redoing the work and hoping the second attempt is luckier.
